- Avoid directory traversal and resource exhaustion when extracting ZIP archives
WHAT: ZIP extraction code can be exploited via directory traversal paths (e.g., "../") or oversized/massive numbers of files, causing writes outside the intended directory or exhausting memory/disk.
WHY: An attacker-controlled archive can overwrite arbitrary files, escape the extraction directory, or consume excessive resources leading to denial of service or data corruption.
HOW: Resolve and validate each member path against a fixed base_path before extraction, rejecting any that do not stay within base_path; enforce strict MAXSIZE and MAXAMT limits on file size and file count using both metadata and actual read size; dimension host RAM/disk to support configured limits.
